 "title": "Treasurer’s Office | Alpena County, MI",
 "text": "Treasurer’s Office | Alpena County, MI\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nDepartments & Services\nCourts\nGovernment\nAbout Us\nHow Do I...\nSearch\nHome\nDepartments & Services\nDepartments\nTreasurer’s Office\nTreasurer’s Office\nThe County Treasurer is the custodian of all county monies. The Treasurer receives revenue from all County departments and prepares a trial balance monthly for each county fund, reconciles the numerous bank accounts, and invests idle county funds and investments. The Treasurer collects all delinquent real property taxes, administers the March settlement (tax monies) with each unit of local government, manages the county's delinquent tax reversion process, and administers the delinquent tax revolving fund. The Treasurer is a member of several County Boards.\nContact Us\nCindy Cebula\nCounty Treasurer\nAmanda Repke\nChief Deputy Treasurer\nRikki Nadeau\nDeputy Treasurer\nTreasurer's Office\ntreasurer@alpenacounty.org\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n720 W Chisholm Street\nSuite 3\nAlpena , MI 49707\n720 W Chisholm Street Suite 3 Alpena MI 49707\nDirections\nPhone: 989-354-9534\nHours\nMonday through Friday\n8 am to 4:30 pm\nLocal Units of Government\nAssessors (PDF)\nTreasurers (PDF)\nDelinquent Property Taxes\nFinancial Hardship\nFinancial Hardship Extension Form (PDF)\nHardship Application (PDF)\nNotice of Intention to Claim Interest in Foreclosure Sale Proceeds (PDF)\nPay Delinquent Taxes Online\nProperty Tax Foreclosure Timeline (PDF)\nPublic Land Auction\nTax Search\nDog Licenses\nDog License Application (PDF)\nService Animals (PDF)\nTransfer of Ownership Form (PDF)\nDog License Information (PDF)\nFee Schedule\nFrequently Asked Questions (PDF)\nBids and RFPs\nAgendas & Minutes\nEmployment\nParks and Recreation\nForms and Permits\nContact Us\n-->\n720 West Chisholm Street\nAlpena, MI 49707\nPhone: 989-354-9500\nFax: 989-354-9648\nAbout Us\nRegister of Deeds\nJob Opportunities\nBuilding Maps\nHome Improvement Program\nEmployee Email\nEmployee Navigator\nPublic Interest\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nThe County Government operates the jail, maintains rural roads, operates the major local courts, keeps files of deeds and mortgages, maintains vital records, administers public health regulations, and participates with the state in the provision of welfare and other social services.\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×",
